# Task 08 — Sticky-Column Pricing Table

**Category:** Data Display
**Difficulty:** advanced
**Style school:** Minimalism

## The problem

A pricing comparison table with many plan columns, where the leftmost
"Feature" column must stay visible while the rest of the table scrolls
horizontally.

## Constraints

- Only one column (`Feature`) is sticky, inside a table that scrolls
  horizontally as a whole.

## Key implementation decisions

- `overflow-x-auto` on the outer wrapper enables horizontal scrolling once
  the plan columns exceed the available width.
- The first `<th>`/`<td>` in every row gets `sticky left-0`, pinning it to
  the left edge of the scroll container during scroll.
- `z-10` is required on the sticky column, not just for polish — without it,
  the other columns' content would visually scroll on top of the pinned
  column instead of staying underneath it.
- The sticky column also needs an explicit background (`bg-white` /
  `bg-neutral-100`) — `sticky` doesn't prevent transparency, so without a
  background the scrolling columns would show through underneath it.
- `min-w-[140px]` on the plan columns guarantees genuine horizontal scrolling
  instead of columns just shrinking to fit.

